# ============================================================================
# Frozen QueryIR bytecode / capture format contract v1 — contract-freeze gate.
#
# Architecture §7 (QueryIR: one engine, multiple dialects), §26 (contract
# freeze), §27 (QUERY lane owns structural/query).
#
# This spec is the gate for the QUERY lane deliverable. Like the ID-TAG and MAP
# gates it proves three separate things, because round-tripping alone is not
# enough for a frozen contract:
#
#   1. EXACT BYTES — encoder output equals a hand-derived golden vector. This is
#      what actually freezes the format; a round-trip test alone passes happily
#      even if encoder and decoder drift together.
#   2. ROUND TRIP — decode(encode(x)) reconstructs x for every record shape.
#   3. REJECTION — malformed, truncated, cross-typed, wrong-version and
#      structurally-invalid buffers are refused rather than silently coerced.
#      For a straight-line op arena this is the important half: an op whose
#      input names a later op does not fail loudly, it evaluates a DIFFERENT
#      query than the one that compiled.
# ============================================================================

